{
  "logo": "https://cdn.uppromote.com/storage/uploads/logo/1770097671_4364381_afe3da043d129b469e86dc0413c87a68.png",
  "description": "<div style=\"font-family:Poppins;\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px auto 1em;max-width:640px;color:rgb(81,89,93);font-family:'Open Sans', sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bold;\">The world needs more quality time.</strong></p><p style=\"margin:1em auto;max-width:640px;color:rgb(81,89,93);font-family:'Open Sans', sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;\">Seeing a parent or spouse age can be an unwelcome surprise. Sometimes, it can actually drive people apart. That’s what happened to Dan, a fellow who bought the American Lifetime Day Clock for his wife of 50 years (#relationshipgoals, right?):</span></p><p style=\"margin:1em auto;max-width:640px;color:rgb(81,89,93);font-family:'Open Sans', sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bold;\"><em>“Every couple of minutes, she would ask me what day it was, what year we were in, was it morning or evening. We love each other dearly, but honestly, it was getting crazy!”</em></strong></p><p style=\"margin:1em auto;max-width:640px;color:rgb(81,89,93);font-family:'Open Sans', sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;\">Can you blame Dan for his frustration? The woman he’s loved longer than many of us have lived was struggling, and it was eating him up. As he started to feel more and more alone, Dan ordered his first Day Clock, and wrote to us about a month later:</span></p><p style=\"margin:1em auto;max-width:640px;color:rgb(81,89,93);font-family:'Open Sans', sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;\"><strong style=\"font-weight:bold;\"><em>“The clock made a striking difference. My wife looks at the wall and feels in control again. Looking forward to another 50 years. Thank you, American Lifetime, you saved this old man’s sanity!”</em></strong></p><p style=\"margin:1em auto;max-width:640px;color:rgb(81,89,93);font-family:'Open Sans', sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;\">I keep a screenshot of Dan’s review on my phone and look at it often. It expresses everything our company stands for: tasteful tools for growing older, quality time spent between spouses, parents and children and a circle of giving </span><span style=\"font-weight:400;\">that will improve the golden years for today’s young adults.</span></p><p style=\"margin:1em auto;max-width:640px;color:rgb(81,89,93);font-family:'Open Sans', sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;\">To many long and bright years,</span></p><p style=\"margin:1em auto;max-width:640px;color:rgb(81,89,93);font-family:'Open Sans', sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;\"><em><span style=\"font-weight:400;\">The American Lifetime Team</span></em></p></div></div>",
